  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildlands Conservation Trust - Sustainable Financing Solutions for 30x30 Implementation in South Africa at both national and  site-specific scales.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marine Protected Areas (MPAs) are essential tools for addressing biodiversity loss and climate change crises, protecting threatened ecosystems and species, while delivering ecosystem services for vulnerable communities. Effectively managed MPAs, aligned to needs of communities, can enhance local socio-economic and ecological resilience to global threats. In 
South Africa, as for many African countries, MPA management is under resourced, reducing conservation effectiveness, the delivery of intended social benefits, and buy-in for MPA expansion. This project aims to counteract this problem by introducing sustainable financing options, and applying MPA funding solutions, while building social license for and confidence in MPA networks as important socio-ecological resilience and risk-reduction tools.</narrative>
  </description>
